  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Caddell Construction Co de obligated $561M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date, across 21 awards with an average award size of $26.7M. Obligations are up 162.7% year over year, reflecting a rebound from prior fiscal swings: FY25 obligations were $214M and FY24 obligations were $979M. Caddell Construction Co de recorded FY23 obligations of $31.1M, FY22 obligations of $2.2B, and FY21 obligations of $231M. The Department of State accounted for the majority of FY2026 to date obligations at $561M, while the Department of Defense obligated $153K. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. The largest buying agency concentration in FY2026 to date suggests contract exposure tied to State Department work. Contract count, average award size, and the year-over-year increase provide a concise picture of the firm’s federal revenue profile so far this fiscal year.",
